   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the Hudson river park act, in relation to defense and\nindemnification obligations relating to the Route 9A bikeway/Greenway adjacent\nto the Hudson river park",
    "basePrintNo": "S6281",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6281-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §7, Chap 592 of 1998",
    "lawSection": "New York City",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6281\n\nSPONSOR: HOYLMAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the Hudson river park act, in relation\nto defense and indemnification obligations relating to the Route 9A\nbikeway/Greenway adjacent to the Hudson river park\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS: OF BILL:\n\nSection 1 of the bill amends paragraph (b) of subdivision 3 of section 7\nof the Hudson River Park Act to add the adjacent Route 9A\nBikeway/Greenway to the existing real property for which New York State\nand New York City are required to provide for insurance, defense and\nindemnification for injuries or property damages that occur in the Park.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Hudson River Park Act requires New York State and New York City,\neach with respect to its real property in Hudson River Park, to either\nself-insure, procure insurance, or reimburse the Hudson River Park Trust\nfor insurance the Trust procures to cover all bodily injury or property\ndamage claims alleged to occur on or relate to the real property of the\nPark.\n\nCurrently, the insurance, defense and indemnification requirements of\nthe Hudson River Park Act do not extend to the Route 9A Bikeway /Green-\nway adjoining the Park, and as a result New York State - the owner of\nthe Bikeway - is not required to defend or indemnify the Trust related\nto claims for personal injury or property damage that occur on the bike-\nway.\n\nOn October 31, 2017, a terrorist attack on the Route 9A bikeway resulted\nin significantly increased insurance coverage costs for the Trust. This\nlegislation would extend the existing insurance coverage, indemnifica-\ntion and defense requirements of the Hudson River Park Act to the bike-\nway to alleviate the burdensome insurance costs on the Trust for inci-\ndents that occur on property owned by New York State.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
